1
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:05,440
(Penny:)Hey. So you guys ready
to order?

2
00:00:05,440 --> 00:00:08,840
(Sheldon:)Since we come in
every Tuesday night at 6:00

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:12,610
(Sheldon:)and order the same exact thing,
and it's now 6:08,

4
00:00:12,610 --> 00:00:15,010
(Sheldon:)I believe your question
not only answers itself

5
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:18,120
(Sheldon:)but also stands alongside
such other nonsensical queries

6
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:23,160
as "Who let the dogs out?"
and, uh, "How are they hanging""

7
00:00:23,160 --> 00:00:25,460
(Penny:)Okay.

8
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:28,160
(Penny:)So, the usual, with extra spit
on Sheldon's hamburger.

9
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,860
(Amy:)Penny, a moment?

10
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:32,400
(Amy:)Do you have plans
this weekend?

11
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:33,600
(Penny:)Oh, gee, Amy, I'm sorry,

12
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:34,900
(Penny:)I'm actually pretty busy
this weekend.

13
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:37,670
(Sheldon:)Probably serving food
that was ordered today.

14
00:00:38,710 --> 00:00:41,010
(Amy:)That's too bad. I was hoping
you could be my plus-one

15
00:00:41,010 --> 00:00:43,180
(Amy:)at the Institute
of Interdisciplinary Studies'

16
00:00:43,180 --> 00:00:45,210
(Amy:)symposium on the impact
of current scientific research

17
00:00:45,210 --> 00:00:46,550
(Amy:)on societal interactions.

18
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:49,550
(Penny:)The what?

19
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,650
(Leonard:)It's an annual
science conference.

20
00:00:52,650 --> 00:00:54,020
(Leonard:)We've all been invited to speak.

21
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:57,260
Oh! Oh, okay, well, you know,
like I said, I have plans, so...

22
00:00:57,260 --> 00:00:59,060
(Amy:)Shame. Since you're
my best friend,

23
00:00:59,060 --> 00:01:01,130
(Amy:)I thought it would be
a good bonding opportunity.

